    "title": "Presentation Tuesday on epic maritime fails",
    "text": "A naval architect will host a presentation about maritime mishaps at 6:30 p.m. Tuesday, Jan. 27, at the library, 26 North Road.\nThe free presentation by Bill Krol, “My Favorite Maritime Epic Fails,” will include eight stories that feature “crazy ideas, lousy design, poor judgement and bad karma.” This is a revised, expanded version of his 2015 presentation.\nKrol, of Portsmouth, started his career working for the U.S. Navy as a shipfitter’s helper at the Norfolk Naval Shipyard in Virginia. He then worked for 33 years at the Naval Undersea Warfare Center in Newport.",
